---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About - Imagile"
  description="Why Imagile exists, how we work, and why we default to Azure and .NET."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <Section eyebrow="About" title="Why Imagile exists">
      <p class="lead about-lead">
        I spent over a decade in enterprise software. Good companies, smart people, complicated systems.
        What I kept bumping into was the distance -- between the people writing the software and the people
        whose problems it was supposed to solve.
      </p>
      <p>
        Big organizations are good at many things. Working directly with clients on hard problems isn't
        usually one of them. So I started Imagile. The pitch isn't complicated: a small, expert team that
        works directly with clients to build software that actually works. No layers. No handoffs to three
        other departments. Just us and the problem.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section tone="panel" eyebrow="How we work" title="Operating principles">
      <div class="principles-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Senior-only, always</h3>
          <p>Every engagement is staffed by the people who actually do the work. No account managers relaying requirements badly, no junior handoffs.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Opinionated, on purpose</h3>
          <p>We have a stack we trust and a way we build. We'll tell you when we think an approach is wrong -- that's part of what you're paying for.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Small, deliberately</h3>
          <p>We stay small enough that nothing gets lost between what a client asked for and what actually ships.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section eyebrow="Stack" title="Why we default to Azure and .NET">
      <p>
        Performance, a real talent pool, and secretless authentication. We wrote the full argument in
        <a href="/blog/why-we-use-azure-and-dotnet">Azure and .NET: The Boring Stack That Wins</a> --
        it's a default, not a dogma, but it's the default for almost every client project.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section align="center" tone="panel">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn" data-track="About_CTA">Start a Conversation</a>
    </Section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-lead {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .principles-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .principles-grid h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .principles-grid p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .principles-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-md);
    }
  }
</style>
